 know who  was in that area  so we believe today from uh we're  talking to our contacts  on the ground to the military as well is  that a suicide bomber has come into that  canal area and has exploded his bomb  there are huge number of people and  there will be casualties amongst them  for certain because it it's impossible  not there is a high wall that leads out  of the canal which would be always  guarded  mainly by american soldiers  we believe that  some are injured and we have been told  that some are dead but we do not know  that now but this was a a choke point a  very dangerous one we don't believe it  would be the taliban we think it is  islamic state and their affiliate with  uh within afghanistan  um there will be casualties for certain  we then heard there was a um what was  described as a firefight to us but we  don't know that could have just been  soldiers firing it could have been other  people firing because it often is like  that when you have uh bomb attacks they  can be very very chaotic i've been in  them that is what they're like there are  reports of a second bomb which would  then suggest we're talking about a  sophisticated attack with a  bomb  gunfire bomb that's fairly standard and  as people run away they get hit by the  second uh bomb or if medical staff or  more soldiers arrive that's the second  bomb now that is only being reported at  the moment but that is sort of usually  how it works if it is a sophisticated  attack  what effect this has  on the whole processing system i think  my suspicion is it could almost be the  end of it because the risk will not go  away it'll actually increase  and  we already know that some countries had  already said the risk is too high and  we're withdrawing anyway  that could be end of it is a hugely  significant event because of that alone  days earlier than the expected  withdrawal which in many ways regardless  of dates was going to be quicker than  probably most afghans who were trying to  get out uh would have hoped but i think  that might be the the effect of this  we'll have to see of course but the the  the main airport itself  by the pentagon standards still has  about ten thousand people in it that  have to be um uh processed um that is  possible i suppose  but they will have to withdraw and they  will have to protect uh the airport now  the airport is absolutely vast and you  can imagine it's not as big as heathrow  but think about the number of people you  would need to protect heathrow or any  big airport that anyone has traveled for  it's vast very very difficult to do so  they'll have to draw in further uh it  means that the whole of this relief  effort the whole of the evacuation is is  probably coming to an end
 

